hermes v0.23.0: model_catalog.openrouter_all_models lists every OpenRouter
model hermes can drive, not only the curated manifest.

The OpenRouter picker list (hermes_cli/models.py fetch_openrouter_models)
is hermes' remote catalog manifest (model_catalog.url,
get_curated_openrouter_models) intersected with the live
https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models catalog and filtered to models that
support tool calling. A model missing from the manifest never shows, on
any surface (e.g. reflection/beam-1.0-501b-a23b; live: 465 models, 401
with tools, the manifest picks ~60).

With `model_catalog.openrouter_all_models: true` the list is the curated
rows first (order and badges unchanged), then every other live model
that advertises `tools` and is not an image/video generator
(chat_catalog.catalog_item_is_generation), sorted by id, badge "free"
where free. Off (the default) the list is upstream's.

Every surface reads this one list: model_ids() and so
provider_model_ids / cached_provider_model_ids("openrouter")
(provider_models_cache.json), which feed list_authenticated_providers and
so build_model_options_payload: the desktop app and the dashboard
(GET /api/model/options), the TUI (model.options), and `hermes model`;
list_picker_providers (the messaging /model picker; openrouter is
uncapped there, Telegram pages, Discord shows the first 75);
curated_models_for_provider; and the bare-name lookup
_find_openrouter_slug (/model beam-1.0-501b-a23b).

Caches: openrouter_curated_catalog.json records which list it holds
("all_models"); a fresh read with the other setting refetches (the
cache-only read path still serves any copy). The in-process slot is
separate per setting. The option is part of _credential_fingerprint
("openrouter"), so provider_models_cache.json's row does not keep serving
the other list for its week-long stale window. Size: ~400 rows, the disk
cache 22 KB, the /api/model/options payload ~50 KB.

Upstream status: not reported; hyperhermes-only option.

